course: dictionary
lesson: 2462
title: Place names and everyday words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names of places. Darjeeling is a town in the hills of north-east India. A place name starts with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence. Words like this are called proper nouns.
explain: The same word can name something you can drink. «A cup of Darjeeling» means a drink of tea, not a town. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: Context gives you clues. «In the 1800s the British started big tea gardens in India, in Assam and Darjeeling» tells you that Darjeeling is a place where tea grows, so here it is a town.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. If «a cup of tea» still makes sense in the sentence, then Darjeeling means the tea. If you are still not sure, a dictionary will settle it.
fact: Darjeeling is a town in the Himalayan hills of West Bengal, in north-east India.
fact: «Darjeeling» is also the name of a light, fragrant black tea grown on the hills.
fact: Darjeeling tea is sometimes called «the champagne of teas».
fact: The «toy train» at Darjeeling is the Darjeeling Himalayan Railway, a UNESCO World Heritage Site.
fact: From the town you can see Kangchenjunga, the third highest mountain in the world.
exercise: «Tea came from China, and in the 1800s the British started big tea gardens in India, in Assam and Darjeeling.» What is Darjeeling in this sentence? | A mountain in China | *A place where tea gardens grow | A type of biscuit | A kind of cup
exercise: «She poured a steaming pot of Darjeeling for her nan.» What is Darjeeling in this sentence? | *A tea | A mountain | A town in India | A railway
exercise: Why does Darjeeling start with a capital letter? | It is a mistake | It is a very important word | It is the first word of a sentence | *It is the name of a place
test: In «the Darjeeling toy train», what does Darjeeling name? | Tea | A song | *A place | A kind of cup
test: Which sentence uses Darjeeling to mean a tea? | *Would you like a cup of Darjeeling? | The toy train climbs the hills of Darjeeling. | Kangchenjunga can be seen from Darjeeling. | Darjeeling is in India.
exam: Ananya reads «a cup of Darjeeling» and thinks it means a town. What is the best check? | *Swap in tea: «a cup of tea» still makes sense, so it means the drink | Count the letters in the word | Look only at the capital letter and decide it must be a place | Assume every word with a capital letter is a town
